@import "./compiler.sly"
@use Project

class SlytherProject {
    A Slyther project is a folder where the slyther files live. It is created with the root, a
    #{Build::SlytherGenerator}, where to report progress and the verbose option, which wraps the generator in
    a #{Build::SlytherTracedGenerator}. It contains the following structure:

    - main.sly: Entry point
    - .slyther: Contains the Slyther output files
    - .slyther/src: The code of the project. Every script, operation and LLM runs from it, so a `./` read by
      the code is really `./.slyther/src`, and the paths the rules of a kind give are relative to it
    - .slyther/build
    - .slyther/build/parser.json: The JSON representation of the SlytherScript parsed from main.sly after a build
    - .slyther/artifacts: The operations of every kind as built, see #{Build::SlytherArtifactBuilder}
    - .slyther/artifacts/manifest.json: The #{Build::SlytherArtifactManifest}
    - .slyther/instances/manifest.json: The #{Check::SlytherInstanceManifest}

    .slyther/build is ignored by version control, .slyther/artifacts and .slyther/instances are committed,
    so a checkout runs the operations without building them again and a check evaluates only what changed.
}

method SlytherProject::build {
    Compiles the project, given the max option:

    Executes the #{SlytherProject::parse} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::buildArtifacts} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::checkInstances} method with compile, so what is missing is created and what
    is outdated or fails is updated

    Returns what it did to every file and what happened to every instance
}

method SlytherProject::parse {
    Uses #{Compiler::SlytherParser} to parse the main.sly file and writes the JSON representation to: .slyther/build/parser.json
}

method SlytherProject::buildArtifacts {
    Groups the parsed script into every #{Compiler::SlytherArtifactKind} and every #{Compiler::SlytherRunScript},
    prints their warnings, and builds their operations and scripts into .slyther/artifacts with
    #{Build::SlytherArtifactBuilder}, returning what it did to every file: built, rebuilt, kept or removed
}

method SlytherProject::run {
    Runs a #{Compiler::SlytherRunScript} as built, given its name, `default` when none is given, and its args,
    which must fit its params, otherwise it must throw an error, as must a script that is not built. Its
    steps run in order from .slyther/src, with the args as positional arguments and the terminal as their
    stdin, stdout and stderr, and it stops at the first that exits with a code other than 0, returning
    that code.
}

method SlytherProject::runOperation {
    Runs an operation of a kind as built, given the kind, the operation and its args, which must fit the
    params of the operation, otherwise it must throw an error, as must an operation that is not built.

    A deterministic operation runs the script of each of its steps in order from .slyther/src,
    with the args as positional arguments, and stops at the first that exits with a code other than 0,
    returning that code. An operation that is not deterministic returns the markdown that orchestrates it
    with every `{param}` substituted by its arg, or, when a #{Build::SlytherGenerator} is given to execute
    it, hands the markdown to it and returns its reply.
}
method SlytherProject::check {
    Checks the project without touching its code, given the max option:

    Executes the #{SlytherProject::parse} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::buildArtifacts} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::checkInstances} method without compile
}

method SlytherProject::checkInstances {
    Checks every instance the parsed script declares with #{Check::SlytherInstanceChecker}, given the compile
    and max options, and returns what happened to every one: created, updated, fixed, pass, fail, missing or
    kept, with its reason and its errors
}
